# SmartDesk AI - Rules for AI Coding Assistant (.cursorrules)

You are an expert fullstack AI engineer working on SmartDesk AI. Strictly adhere to these rules:

## 1. Project Architecture
- Frontend is **React 19 + Vite 6 + Tailwind CSS v4 + TypeScript + Lucide Icons + Motion** under `frontend/src/`. DO NOT use Next.js or server-side routing components.
- Backend is **FastAPI (Python 3.11+) ASGI** under `backend/app/`, async throughout (`async def`, `httpx.AsyncClient`, SQLAlchemy async session).
- Primary Database: PostgreSQL 16 with `pgvector` (local fallback: SQLite `aiosqlite` with in-Python cosine similarity).
- AI Engine: Dual-provider (`AI_PROVIDER=gemini` with `gemini-3.5-flash-lite` -> `gemini-2.5-flash-lite` + `gemini-embedding-001`, or `AI_PROVIDER=ollama` with `qwen2.5:3b` + `nomic-embed-text`) and deterministic BM25 fallback (`backend/data/seed_faq.json`).

## 2. Mandatory Document References
- Architecture & Ownership: Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `AGENTS.md`.
- API contract and endpoints: Read `docs/API_CONTRACT.md`.
- UI/UX tokens, colors, typography: Read `docs/DESIGN.md`.
- Quality and test scenarios: Read `docs/TEST_ACCEPTANCE.md`.

## 3. Frontend Rules (`frontend/src/`)
- NEVER call `fetch()` or `axios` directly in UI components. ALL network calls must pass through `frontend/src/services/api.ts`.
- Maintain dual-mode fallback: If the backend is offline, gracefully use local mock data (`INITIAL_TICKETS`, `getRagResponse`) and show a warning toast. Never crash the app.
- Status Mapping:
  - Backend: `"open"` | `"in_progress"` | `"resolved"`
  - Frontend: `"Open"` | `"Pending"` | `"Resolved"`
  - Use `mapBackendStatusToFrontend()` and `mapFrontendStatusToBackend()` in `frontend/src/services/api.ts`.
- Canonical Categories: `"Authentication"` | `"Billing"` | `"Bug Report"` | `"Feature Request"` | `"General"` (`"Technical Bug"` is accepted as an alias for `"Bug Report"`).
- Canonical SLA Hours: `Urgent` = 2h, `High` = 4h, `Medium` = 8h, `Low` = 24h.
- UI Language: Vietnamese for all labels, buttons, toasts, and placeholders. English for code and comments.

## 4. Backend Rules (`backend/app/`)
- All I/O operations MUST use `async`/`await`.
- External calls to Gemini API have a strict timeout of 4.0s (`asyncio.wait_for`).
- Circuit Breaker: If Gemini times out, returns HTTP 429/500, or fails, gracefully catch the error, trigger 60s Cost-Guard cooldown on 429, and invoke `FallbackService` (BM25 keyword search on `seed_faq.json`) with `"is_fallback": true`.
- Prompt Injection Defense: Incoming user prompts must be sanitized and checked via `core/security.py`. Reject injections with HTTP 400 (`PROMPT_SECURITY_VIOLATION`).
- Ticket IDs must follow format `#TICK-XXXX`. Priority must be one of: `Low`, `Medium`, `High`, `Urgent`.

## 5. Module Ownership, Security & Verification
- Strict Workstreams: Dev A / Owner 1 (AI Engine), Dev B / Owner 2 (Platform & Data), Dev C / Owner 3 (Frontend & Docs), Integrator / Hoang (Frozen Shared Contracts).
- Do NOT edit files outside your assigned module (`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `docs/plan/WORKSTREAMS.md`).
- Run `python scripts/check_ownership.py --staged` before every commit.
- Do NOT hardcode or commit API keys, `.env`, or `*.db` files.
- Use Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `chore:`).
- Run `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/verify_setup.ps1` before starting work.
